W: 1. I am a weaver, a Calton weaver
W: I am a brash and a roving blade
W: I have silver in my pouches
W: And I follow a roving trade.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Whiskey, whiskey, Nancy Whiskey
W: Whiskey, whiskey, Nancy O.
W:
W: 2. As I walked into Glasgow city
W: Nancy Whiskey I chanced to smell
W: I walked in, sat down beside her
W: Seven long years I loved her well.
W:
W: 3. The more I kissed her, the more I loved her
W: The more I kissed her, the more she smiled
W: I forgot my mother's teaching
W: Nancy soon had me beguiled.
W:
W: 4. I woke early in the mornin'
W: Tae slake ma drought it was my need,
W: I tried to rise but was not able
W: Nancy had me by the heid.
W:
W: 5. Come landlady, noo, what's that lawin'?
W: Tell me what there is tae pay.
W: "Fifteen shillings is the reck'ning;
W: Noo pay me quickly and go away!"
W:
W: 6. I'll gang back to the Calton weaving
W: I'll surely mak those shuttles fly
W: I'll make more at the Calton weaving
W: Than ever I did in a roving way.
W:
W: 7. So come all ye weavers, ye Calton weavers
W: Weavers where e're ye be
W: Beware of Whiskey, Nancy Whiskey
W: She'll ruin you like she ruined me.
